{"lines": ["The Army said it had captured a flying disc. A day later, it took that back.", "On a New Mexico ranch, Mac Brazel found tinfoil, rubber and sticks.", "The nearby air base put out a press release: a flying disc, recovered.", "But in Fort Worth, General Roger Ramey showed reporters the debris. A weather balloon, he said.", "For thirty-one years, it went quiet. Then Major Jesse Marcel, who gathered the debris, called it a cover story.", "Later books added alien bodies. So the Air Force reopened its files.", "Its nineteen ninety-four report named Project Mogul, most likely: secret balloon trains built to hear Soviet atomic tests.", "The purple 'symbols' people recalled matched flower-printed tape from a toy maker.", "Mogul was secret. The weather balloon stood in.", "For forty-seven years, that stayed the answer. Nobody explained it."], "words": [["The", 0.0, 0.1], ["Army", 0.1, 0.32], ["said", 0.32, 0.62], ["it", 0.62, 0.74], ["had", 0.74, 0.84], ["captured", 0.84, 1.2], ["a", 1.2, 1.4], ["flying", 1.4, 1.66], ["disc.", 1.66, 2.04], ["A", 2.54, 2.68], ["day", 2.68, 2.82], ["later,", 2.82, 3.14], ["it", 3.14, 3.36], ["took", 3.36, 3.5], ["that", 3.5, 3.68], ["back.", 3.68, 3.96], ["On", 4.48, 4.52], ["a", 4.52, 4.6], ["New", 4.6, 4.72], ["Mexico", 4.72, 5.1], ["ranch,", 5.1, 5.46], ["Mac", 5.98, 6.24], ["Brazel", 6.24, 6.82], ["found", 6.82, 7.1], ["tinfoil,", 7.1, 7.86], ["rubber", 8.12, 8.36], ["and", 8.7, 8.74], ["sticks.", 8.74, 9.02], ["The", 9.9, 9.94], ["nearby", 9.94, 10.16], ["air", 10.16, 10.54], ["base", 10.54, 10.76], ["put", 10.76, 11.04], ["out", 11.04, 11.18], ["a", 11.18, 11.26], ["press", 11.26, 11.44], ["release:", 11.44, 11.86], ["a", 12.36, 12.46], ["flying", 12.46, 12.7], ["disc,", 12.7, 13.16], ["recovered.", 13.44, 13.72], ["But", 14.36, 14.4], ["in", 14.4, 14.5], ["Fort", 14.5, 14.74], ["Worth,", 14.74, 15.04], ["General", 15.48, 15.72], ["Roger", 15.72, 16.08], ["Ramey", 16.08, 16.62], ["showed", 16.62, 16.9], ["reporters", 16.9, 17.